1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
Every NBA season is a raw boxscore — noisy, pace-biased.

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:04,200
We keep MIN ≥ 800 — about ten minutes per game minimum.

3
00:00:04,200 --> 00:00:06,500
Per-100 possession strips pace — points, assists, rebounds.

4
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:08,800
Era-z normalizes fourteen dimensions — subtract era mean, divide sigma.

5
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:11,200
Cleaning: dedup PID plus season, keep rookies, split Jr and Sr by name plus dob.

6
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:14,000
Result — twelve thousand nine sixty six careers on a fourteen-d unit input.
